<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the hardened runtime (codesign option "runtime"). Deliberately empty.

  The app is distributed with a Developer ID, not through the App Store, so it is not
  sandboxed and none of the com.apple.security.app-sandbox family applies. Under the
  hardened runtime alone, what it uses needs nothing extra:

  - CoreBluetooth (central role). The hardened runtime has no Bluetooth entitlement;
    com.apple.security.device.bluetooth is a sandbox entitlement. Access is a TCC prompt,
    driven by NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription in Info.plist, which is all a
    non-sandboxed app needs.
  - CoreMIDI virtual source and destination. No entitlement or TCC prompt.
  - WKWebView (Wails v2 on macOS). JavaScript runs and JITs in WebKit's own
    com.apple.WebKit.WebContent process, which Apple signs, so this process needs neither
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit nor allow-unsigned-executable-memory. (Electron needs
    allow-jit because V8 runs in the app process; Wails does not embed V8.)
  - The Go runtime and cgo. Go does not generate code at run time. Every Mach-O in the
    bundle is ours and signed with the same identity, so library validation can stay on.
  - "Reveal in Finder" (logs) runs /usr/bin/open, a separate Apple-signed process, so no
    com.apple.security.automation.apple-events either.

  If a future feature needs one (a microphone, Apple Events to another app), add the key
  here and say why next to it. The same file is used for local and ad-hoc builds, so a
  missing entitlement shows up in `make app` before it reaches a release.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
